#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096746 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096547 :question/id #uuid "8de46974-719c-5ac2-a43c-83d1c67c57b6" :question/math-academy-id "e-6234" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-6y+2z &=8 \\\\ -6x+18y-6z &=-24 \\\\ 4x-12y+4z &=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n\n$$\nM= \\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -6 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 18 & -6 & -24 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4 & 16\\end{array} \\right].\n$$\n\n\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -6 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 18 & -6 & -24 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -6 & 18 & -6 & -24 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 4 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa91091b-5368-5d80-b87d-08b3524177f3" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610200 :question-generator/id #uuid "ab9ac0f6-90ff-5bbd-bc14-8265399b754c" :question-generator/script "generators/4d/4dec2fe260850973d7781415bb0decc28f4e58f784f41f8ed5fd703de904df82/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097355 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e96cae01-9e4c-550e-a03c-05da434a1e52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 + z \\\\ 2z \\\