equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-8y-12z &=-44 \\\\ 3x-6y-9z &=-33 \\\\ 4x-8y-12z &=-44\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & -8 & -12 & -44 \\\\ 3 & -6 & -9 & -33 \\\\ 4 & -8 & -12 & -44\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1:=\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 3 & -6 & -9 & -33 \\\\ 4 & -8 & -12 & -44\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-3)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -8 & -12 & -44\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(-4)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610180 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b2a5f2c-538e-5e01-b631-2f843e33e59c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610165} {:answer/id #uuid "82a14710-0b79-52cc-b360-38bbf1cf3cfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & 1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610181} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5bab5e-af82-5896-bd45-a75c3bb3c3c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610185} {:answer/id #uuid "adeddc92-21df-5913-b3b9-1eb1481d0ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610186} {:answer/id #uuid "b5cc6758-b727-5e89-b37d-58a3780d5831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adeddc92-21df-5913-b3b9-1eb1481d0ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610186} :answer-field/id #uuid "75e8462a-a3c5-52db-94ed-d477e9e685d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610179}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7afe353a-d416-5657-a26d-0489dcb2d4a8" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x-20y+5z &=70 \\\\ x+4y-z &=-14 \\\\ -9x-36y+9z &=126\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-5 & -20 & 5 & 70 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -9 & -36 & 9 & 126\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1\\leftrightarrow R_2\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -1 & -14 \\\\ -5 & -20 & 5 & 70 \\\\ -9 & -36 & 9 & 126\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(5)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -9 & -36 & 9 & 126\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(9)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 4 & -1 & -14 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186610191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "259a5c2b-98a7-5fac-b64c-563253aa4bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -2 & -17 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610169} {:answer/id #uuid "355f8589-770b-5c39-8f8d-a2d3b0938ed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & -17 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610173} {:answer/id #uuid "8335e7fa-5847-53ec-a657-a7a51d2a4d79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 & -17 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610182} {:answer/id #uuid "d8864bd4-414c-524f-a318-375eb2a3b27b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -17 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610193} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a3b200-3cc0-54ce-89f0-8d9388c172f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & 17 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "355f8589-770b-5c39-8f8d-a2d3b0938ed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 2 & -17 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610173} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5592f1-32c0-5239-ab52-de8476a3a6c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186610167}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2f58ab6-d1b7-50da-b3ff-00d8364d5812" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-4y+4z &=-34 \\\\ -9x+18y-18z &=153 \\\\ -7x+14y-14z &=119\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & -4 & 4 & -34 \\\\ -9 & 18 & -18 & 153 \\\\ -7 & 14 & -14 & 119\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1:=\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -17 \\\\ -9 & 18 & -18 & 153 \\\\ -7 & 14 & -14 & 119\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(9)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -17 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 14 & -14 & 119\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(7)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & -17 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186642325 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f511ec6-1939-5219-84f4-e2c01af54ee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+y-2z \\\\ y-2z \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186641979} {:answer/id #uuid "b710ae49-a066-5526-a402-abe00927ed81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}y-2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642099} {:answer/id #uuid "e141920d-9672-5616-8cef-f3bc91bb19f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1-y+2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642156} {:answer/id #uuid "f65eab76-8773-55a7-a672-b394513cd468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+y-2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642182} {:answer/id #uuid "ff40d920-51f2-508e-959d-73447112cefd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1-y+2z \\\\ y \\\\ 1+y\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f65eab76-8773-55a7-a672-b394513cd468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1+y-2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642182} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1c589bd-79b4-5cb6-b6f5-030646954caf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186642275}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "693512da-f45c-5aae-999f-b43069296756" :question/math-academy-id "q-74614" :question/problem "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8x-8y+16z &=8 \\\\ -8x+8y-16z &=-8 \\\\ 16x-16y+32z &=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -8 & 16 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 8 & -16 & -8 \\\\ 16 & -16 & 32 & 16\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -8 & 16 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 8 & -16 & -8 \\\\ 16 & -16 & 32 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -8 & 8 & -16 & -8 \\\\ 16 & -16 & 32 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 16 & -16 & 32 & 16\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+16{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z &=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations, we can remove these equations from the system. \n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables, $y,$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1+y-2z \\\\ y &=y \\\\ z &=z,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere $y$ and $z$ (the free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1+y-2z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix},\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a Singular 3x3 System With One Pivot"}]}
